/** @mainpage Qore xmlsec Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section xmlsecintro Introduction to the xmlsec Module

    The xmlsec module provides <a href="https://www.aleksey.com/xmlsec/">xmlsec</a> functionality
    to Qore, allowing qore programs to generate and verify XML documents with signatures and
    encryption.

    This module is released under a choice of two licenses:
    - <a href="http://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html">LGPL 2.1</a>
    - MIT (see COPYING.MIT in the source distribution for more information)
    .
    The module is tagged as such in the module's header (meaning it can be loaded unconditionally
    regardless of how the %Qore library was initialized).

    Like all Qore components, the xmlsec module is thread-safe.

    Encryption, decryption, signing, and verification is performed through the static methods of the
    @ref Qore::XmlSec::XmlSec "XmlSec" class, while access to keys and key managers is provided through
    the @ref Qore::XmlSec::XmlSecKey "XmlSecKey" and @ref Qore::XmlSec::XmlSecKeyManager "XmlSecKeyManager"
    classes.

    @section xmlsec_examples Usage Examples

    @subsection xmlsec_sign_verify Signing and Verifying XML

    @par Example: Sign an XML Document
    @code{.py}
%requires xmlsec
%requires xml

# Create a key from a PEM file
XmlSecKey key(File::readTextFile("private-key.pem"), xmlSecKeyDataFormatPem, "password");
key.setCertificate(File::readTextFile("certificate.pem"), xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertPem);

# Create the signature template (using the xml module)
hash sig_template = {
    "Document": {
        "Data": "content to sign",
        "Signature": {
            "^attributes^": {"xmlns": "http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#"},
            "SignedInfo": {
                "CanonicalizationMethod": {
                    "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/TR/2001/REC-xml-c14n-20010315"},
                },
                "SignatureMethod": {
                    "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmldsig-more#rsa-sha256"},
                },
                "Reference": {
                    "^attributes^": {"URI": ""},
                    "Transforms": {
                        "Transform": {
                            "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#enveloped-signature"},
                        },
                    },
                    "DigestMethod": {
                        "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#sha256"},
                    },
                    "DigestValue": NOTHING,
                },
            },
            "SignatureValue": NOTHING,
            "KeyInfo": {
                "X509Data": NOTHING,
            },
        },
    },
};

# Sign the template
string signed_xml = XmlSec::sign(make_xml(sig_template), key);
    @endcode

    @par Example: Verify a Signed XML Document
    @code{.py}
# Verify using the same key (or public key/certificate)
try {
    XmlSec::verify(signed_xml, key);
    printf("Signature is valid\n");
} catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    printf("Signature verification failed: %s\n", ex.desc);
}
    @endcode

    @subsection xmlsec_encrypt_decrypt Encrypting and Decrypting XML

    @par Example: Encrypt Data with a Session Key
    @code{.py}
# Create a session key for AES encryption
XmlSecKey session_key(xmlSecKeyDataAesId, 256, xmlSecKeyDataTypeSession);

# Create certificate key for encrypting the session key
XmlSecKey cert_key(File::readTextFile("private-key.pem"), xmlSecKeyDataFormatPem, "password");
cert_key.setCertificate(File::readTextFile("certificate.pem"), xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertPem);

# Set up key manager
XmlSecKeyManager mgr();
mgr.addKey(cert_key);

# Create encryption template
hash enc_template = {
    "EncryptedData": {
        "^attributes^": {
            "xmlns": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#",
            "Type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#Element",
        },
        "EncryptionMethod": {
            "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#aes256-cbc"},
        },
        "KeyInfo": {
            "^attributes^": {"xmlns": "http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#"},
            "EncryptedKey": {
                "^attributes^": {"xmlns": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#"},
                "EncryptionMethod": {
                    "^attributes^": {"Algorithm": "http://www.w3.org/2001/04/xmlenc#rsa-1_5"},
                },
                "KeyInfo": {
                    "^attributes^": {"xmlns": "http://www.w3.org/2000/09/xmldsig#"},
                    "X509Data": NOTHING,
                },
                "CipherData": {"CipherValue": NOTHING},
            },
        },
        "CipherData": {"CipherValue": NOTHING},
    },
};

# Encrypt the data
string encrypted_xml = XmlSec::encrypt("<SensitiveData>secret</SensitiveData>",
    make_xml(enc_template), session_key, mgr);
    @endcode

    @par Example: Decrypt Encrypted XML
    @code{.py}
# Decrypt using the key manager (which contains the private key)
data decrypted = XmlSec::decrypt(encrypted_xml, mgr);
    @endcode

    @section xmlsec_key_types Supported Key Types

    The module supports the following key types through the @ref xmlsec_keydataid_constants:
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataAesId "xmlSecKeyDataAesId" - AES symmetric keys
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataDesId "xmlSecKeyDataDesId" - DES symmetric keys
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataDsaId "xmlSecKeyDataDsaId" - DSA keys
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataHmacId "xmlSecKeyDataHmacId" - HMAC keys
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataRsaId "xmlSecKeyDataRsaId" - RSA keys
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataX509Id "xmlSecKeyDataX509Id" - X.509 certificates

    Keys can be loaded from various formats using @ref xmlsec_keydataformat_constants:
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatPem "xmlSecKeyDataFormatPem" - PEM format
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatDer "xmlSecKeyDataFormatDer" - DER format
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs8Pem "xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs8Pem" - PKCS#8 PEM
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs8Der "xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs8Der" - PKCS#8 DER
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs12 "xmlSecKeyDataFormatPkcs12" - PKCS#12
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertPem "xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertPem" - Certificate PEM
    - @ref Qore::XmlSec::xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertDer "xmlSecKeyDataFormatCertDer" - Certificate DER

    @section xmlsec_errors Error Handling

    All methods throw exceptions on error. The following exception types may be raised:
    - \c XMLSEC-SIGN-ERROR - Error during XML signing
    - \c XMLSEC-VERIFY-ERROR - Signature verification failed
    - \c XMLSEC-ENCRYPT-ERROR - Error during XML encryption
    - \c XMLSEC-DECRYPT-ERROR - Error during XML decryption
    - \c XMLSEC-DSIGCTX-ERROR - Digital signature context error
    - \c XMLSECKEY-ERROR - Key-related error
    - \c XMLSECKEYMANAGER-ERROR - Key manager error

